+# Feature Specification: Availability Query
+
+**Created**: 2026-10-21 | **Status**: Draft
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - See what can still be rented (P1)
+Desk staff give a period, and optionally a kind, and see at a glance which equipment is free for the whole period.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board and a sail, none booked, when asking for a period without kind, both ids are returned, sorted.
+2. Given a kind (`board`), only equipment of that kind is returned.
+3. Given an item with a booking overlapping the period, even partly, it is not returned.
+4. Given a booking that ends where the period starts (or starts where it ends), the item is returned.
+5. Given nothing is free, an empty list is returned.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- Invalid period (not UTC midnights, empty, reversed, non-ISO): rejected, as for `quote`.
+- Invalid kind (not `board`/`sail`): rejected.
+- Querying never changes stored equipment or bookings.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `availability({ start, end, kind? })` is added to the rental service.
+- **FR-002**: Period rules are those of FR-003 of the rental module (midnight UTC, start < end, end exclusive).
+- **FR-003**: Returns the ids of equipment free for the whole period: no booking of the item overlaps it (same overlap rule as `book`).
+- **FR-004**: When `kind` is given only equipment of that kind is considered; otherwise all kinds.
+- **FR-005**: Ids are returned sorted ascending (plain string order) in a new array.
+- **FR-006**: Throws for an invalid period or an invalid `kind`.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: An id is returned exactly when `book` for the same item and period would succeed.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Omitted (`undefined`) kind means any kind.
+- Only existing bookings count; cancellation remains out of scope.
